# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Quoril desktop (Electron) environment — copy to `.env` and fill in.
# Client-side secrets are Supabase-only, matching the Quoril-Swift app: both
# apps share one Supabase project, and every third-party key (NVIDIA, Slack)
# lives in Supabase Edge Function secrets, never in the client.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Supabase project (public — safe in the client; RLS enforces access).
# Only the VITE_SUPABASE_* prefix is exposed to the renderer (see vite.config.ts).
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://izxoyfydqsopvaywrtuz.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_XTpgjyAzkWJJ5RwysjRZlg_4jjsZV4Q

# --- AI Insights -----------------------------------------------------------
# Primary AI backend is the `quoril-insights` Supabase Edge Function (NVIDIA
# Nemotron). Its NVIDIA_API_KEY is a Supabase function secret, NOT set here:
#   supabase secrets set NVIDIA_API_KEY=...
#
# Fallback only (server-side; never shipped to the renderer): the legacy Groq
# path via the landing site. Leave unset if you don't run the fallback.
# GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...
# QUORIL_INSIGHTS_URL=https://www.quoril.in/api/insights

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The following are NOT app env vars — they are Supabase Edge Function secrets,
# set with `supabase secrets set ...`, listed here for reference only:
#   NVIDIA_API_KEY          (quoril-insights)
#   SLACK_CLIENT_ID         (slack-integration)
#   SLACK_CLIENT_SECRET     (slack-integration)
#   SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET    (slack-events)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
